An IndexedDB open or delete request in Ladybird waits until the one
before it in its connection queue has completed, upgrade included. So
do the other engines: Chromium’s ConnectionCoordinator keeps an open
request first in request_queue_ until OnUpgradeTransactionFinished().
WebKit’s UniqueIDBDatabase::handleDatabaseOperations() takes no next
open request while a version-change transaction runs. And Gecko’s
FactoryOp::MustWaitFor() holds back an operation for a database while
any other operation for it is still running.
